The '''2024–25 season''' was the 101st season in the history of '''[[Rayo Vallecano]]''', and the club's fourth consecutive season in [[La Liga]]. In addition to the [[2024–25 La Liga|domestic league]], the club participated in the [[2024–25 Copa del Rey|Copa del Rey]].

Rayo Vallecano concluded the La Liga season in eighth place, marking their best league finish since the [[2012–13 La Liga|2012–13 campaign]], when they also secured the same position. This achievement qualified the club for a spot in the [[2025–26 UEFA Conference League|UEFA Conference League]], signaling their return to European competition after a [[2000–01 UEFA Cup|24-year absence]].<ref>https://www.football-espana.net/2025/05/24/rayo-vallecano-24-year-wait-european-return-celta-vigo</ref>

